           are SCE-recognised synonyms in line with analyzer.rs (the same
           three forms register as `has_wildcard`) and parser.rs (the
           same three forms bypass event-name validation). They all
           collapse to "match every non-NONE event" — eventless
           transitions are dispatched separately via EVENT_NONE so the
           wildcard must NOT pick them up, otherwise check_eventless_transitions
           would loop forever. Codegen-time enumeration of all model events
           would also be correct here but would scale linearly with
           model.events; the EVENT_NONE inequality is O(1) regardless. #}
        if (event != {{ model.name | upper }}_EVENT_NONE)
{% elif trans.prefix_matching_events | length == 0 %}
        {# Defensive — analyzer.rs::build_prefix_matching always populates
           prefix_matching_events for non-empty descriptors; an empty list
           means none of the model's events satisfy the descriptor (e.g.
           a `<transition event="never_raised"/>` with no matching raise/
           send). Unreachable in well-formed SCXML, kept as a guard. #}
        if (0)
{% elif trans.prefix_matching_events | length == 1 %}
        if (event == {{ model.name | upper }}_EVENT_{{ trans.prefix_matching_events[0] | upper | replace('.', '_') | replace('-', '_') }})
{% else %}
        {# W3C SCXML 5.9.3: descriptor expansion — covers (a) single-token
